# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Course material that is not ours to publish.
#
# curriculum/tut holds the learning outcomes and assessment criteria of
# Principles of Programming A and B at the Tshwane University of Technology.
# That is departmental material. The model in model/ is the contribution and is
# published; the curriculum is not. curriculum/example is invented and IS
# committed, so that this repository builds and runs for anyone.
#
# See curriculum/README.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
curriculum/tut/
curriculum/*/
!curriculum/example/
!curriculum/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. All of it is reproducible from the model and a curriculum, so
# none of it belongs in the repository — and the knowledge base would carry the
# curriculum's text with it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
build/kb.db
build/d1-seed.sql
build/inferred.ttl
build/build_report.json
build/parity_report.json
api/test/kb.test.db

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Node
node_modules/
web/dist/
.wrangler/
npm-debug.log*
.vite/

# Evaluation output, kept out until Chapter 6 decides what is reported
evaluation/output/

# Patches exchanged while working. They are a transport, not part of the
# project, and committing them puts every change in the repository twice.
*.patch

# Editors and operating systems
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
docs/server.log
docs/server.log.err
docs/evaluation/
